          "unmapped": {
            "result": "# Subagent Definitions and Configuration\n\nBased on the Claude Code documentation, here's what you need to know about subagent definitions:\n\n## File Locations\n\nSubagents can be defined in two ways:\n\n1. **Filesystem-based**: `.claude/agents/*.md` files in your project\n2. **Programmatic**: Defined directly in code (Agent SDK)\n\n## Frontmatter Schema\n\nSubagent files use YAML frontmatter to configure behavior. Key fields include:\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: agent-name\nmodel: claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\nscope: project  # or 'global'\ndescription: What this agent does\ntools:\n  - read\n  - write\n  - bash\npermissions: plan  # permission mode\n---\n```\n\n### Supported Frontmatter Fields\n\nFrom the documentation on **\"Configure subagents\"**:\n\n- **`name`**: The subagent's identifier\n- **`model`**: Which Claude model to use\n- **`scope`**: `project` (repository-specific) or `global` (all projects)\n- **`description`**: What the agent specializes in\n- **`tools`**: Array of available tools (read, write, bash, etc.)\n- *…[TRUNCATED]"
